{"path":"filesystem/recursive_directory_iterator/pop","title":"std::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::pop","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::</span>pop","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/filesystem/recursive_directory_iterator/pop","section":"filesystem","kind":"page","summary":"Moves the iterator one level up in the directory hierarchy. Invalidates all copies of the previous value of *this.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> pop<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> pop<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Moves the iterator one level up in the directory hierarchy. Invalidates all copies of the previous value of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>. \n</p><p>If the parent directory is outside directory hierarchy that is iterated on (i.e. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">depth<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span></span></code>), sets <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> to an end directory iterator.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> error code to store the error status to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Any overload not marked <code>noexcept</code> may throw <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\">std::bad_alloc</a></span> if memory allocation fails.<br>\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Throws <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/filesystem/filesystem_error\">std::filesystem::filesystem_error</a></span> on underlying OS API errors, constructed with  the OS error code as the error code argument.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Sets a <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code\"><span class=\"kw881\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_code</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter to the OS API error code if an OS API call fails, and executes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec.</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_code/clear\"><code>clear</code></a><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> if no errors occur.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"filesystem","title":"Filesystem library (since C++17)"},{"path":"filesystem/recursive_directory_iterator","title":"std::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::pop","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++17. Moves the iterator one level up in the directory hierarchy. Invalidates all copies of the previous value of *this."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Any overload not marked noexcept may throw std::bad_alloc if memory allocation fails."},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":132,"codeBlockCount":0}
